          "text": "{\n  \"target_identification\": {\n    \"speaker\": \"Unnamed first-person narrator\",\n    \"addressee\": \"Maria\",\n    \"anchor_quote\": \"Saavist som jeg altid hellere har sagt Dig for lidt\\nend for meget, saavist elsker jeg Dig. Jeg elsker Dig i Lyst og i\\nNød, Hverdage og Festdage. Du er den, jeg vil dø med, men først vil\\njeg leve meget, meget længe med Dig. Javel har jeg længtes efter\\nmin yndige Elskerindes Kærtegn. Men mest har jeg længtes efter alt\\ndet andet, som ogsaa er Dig: dit trofaste Hjærte, din rene Tanke,\\ndin milde Tale, dit lyse Smil, som er min Sol i Tvivlen, dit gode\\nHaandtryk, som er min Styrke paa Vejen.\"\n  },\n  \"target_translation\": \"I love you.\",\n  \"dimensions\": {\n    \"T\": {\n      \"score\": 4,\n      \"evidence_status\": \"assessable\",\n      \"confidence\": 0.99,\n      \"reason\": \"The focal expression directly avows the speaker's present love for Maria. Its truth-presenting force is strengthened by the solemn 'as surely ... as surely' construction and by its direct answer to Maria's concern that his feeling may be temporary or imagined.\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"block_id\": \"target\",\n          \"quotation\": \"elsker jeg Dig\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"block_id\": \"scene\",\n          \"quotation\": \"Saavist som jeg altid hellere har sagt Dig for lidt\\nend for meget, saavist elsker jeg Dig.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    \"P\": {\n      \"score\": 3,\n      \"evidence_status\": \"assessable\",\n      \"confidence\": 0.91,\n      \"reason\": \"Although the marked words are lexically an avowal, this occurrence is embedded in a solemn response affirming an enduring bond. The immediate continuation defines loving Maria as remaining with her through joy, hardship, ordinary days and celebrations, and sharing a life until death. Thus the focal avowal helps affirm a durable relational undertaking rather than merely sitting beside an unrelated promise. The exact practical or formal terms of that undertaking are not specified.\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"block_id\": \"scene\",\n          \"quotation\": \"Saavist som jeg altid hellere har sagt Dig for lidt\\nend for meget, saavist elsker jeg Dig. Jeg elsker Dig i Lyst og i\\nNød, Hverdage og Festdage. Du er den, jeg vil dø med, men først vil\\njeg leve meget, meget længe med Dig.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    \"E\": {\n      \"score\": 0,\n      \"evidence_status\": \"assessable\",\n      \"confidence\": 0.94,\n      \"reason\": \"The expression is affectively intense, but it is represented as a considered answer to Maria's explicit question, followed by an articulated account of enduring love. The evidence does not present it as a reflex-like or uncontrolled expressive discharge.\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"block_id\": \"scene\",\n          \"quotation\": \"Jeg svarer: »Saavist som jeg altid hellere har sagt Dig for lidt\\nend for meget, saavist elsker jeg Dig.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    \"O\": {\n      \"score\": 0,\n      \"evidence_status\": \"assessable\",\n      \"confidence\": 0.9,\n      \"reason\": \"The focal expression's core work is adequately captured by avowal and its contextual affirmation of an enduring bond. Its reassurance of Maria operates through those truth-presenting and undertaking forces rather than constituting a distinct residual mode.\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"block_id\": \"scene\",\n          \"quotation\": \"For det er jo sandt, ikke noget, Du imorgen fortryder, ikke\\nnoget, Du nu bilder Dig ind, fordi Du har længtes en Smule efter din\\nElskerinde?\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"block_id\": \"target\",\n          \"quotation\": \"elsker jeg Dig\"\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  },\n  \"original_speech_situation\": \"At an emotionally intense reunion, Maria asks whether the narrator's apparent change is genuine, lasting, and not merely caused by temporary longing. He answers her directly with the focal avowal, solemnly guarantees it, and immediately describes his love as enduring through hardship and extending across a shared life.\",\n  \"affection_evidence\": \"present\",\n  \"undertaking_and_uptake\": \"The speaker affirms an enduring partnership: loving Maria in joy and hardship, on ordinary and festive days, and living with her for a long time until death. Maria's tears and happiness are represented as understanding and accepting the truth of his response, although no formal promise, marriage proposal, or fully specified obligations are stated.\",\n  \"recognised_work\": false,\n  \"recognition_note\": \"I do not recognise the work from the supplied evidence.\",\n  \"limitations\": \"The passage strongly represents the avowal as sincere and received as true, but it does not specify a formal status for the relationship or the precise practical obligations created by the affirmation. Nothing can be concluded here about events outside the supplied passage.\"\n}"
